<http://data.silknow.org/object/7c378201-afcb-3143-a742-59b4dd60e92f/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Rectangular ivory colored silk ground with polychrome floss silk yarns worked mainly satin stitch. Four designs in a lengthwise row; two trees flanking a partially embroidered funery monument with the initials \"AB\" and the date in pencil; ruined archways with foliage; an urn with a large naturalistic floral sparay; a mound with trees, a grave and the words \"Auch (?) hier\" on a cross. Naturalistic floral vine border with ivy and oak leaves, acorns, morning glories and other blossoms.  Stained and soiled.   Stitches: couching, French knot, running, satin, shaded stain, stem."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/7c378201-afcb-3143-a742-59b4dd60e92f> .

<https://sws.geonames.org/6255148/>
